Size: content without the on-device model service where it is off.

The on-device model service runs the language models behind Chrome's
built-in AI APIs, and its utility process prepares the GPU through Dawn
before it is sandboxed. use_on_device_model_service says where it is
built, but content's utility process links the service and its sandbox
setup whatever it says, and Dawn with them: 3 MiB, and the SPIR-V tools
under it, in an engine without WebGPU. This links them only where the
service is on. The content shell has no model to run in it.

Off in profiles/slim.gn. Upstream's default is unchanged.

